    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0535" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.91/1–1145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of
                            State to the Director of the Office of Near Eastern and African
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-02">January 2, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Iranian Free Port and Railroad Trusteeship</p>
                <p>Thank you for your memorandum of the 20th [<hi rendition="#italic">30th?</hi>].
                    When I was with the President on Saturday<anchor n="61" xml:id="d510-f1"/> I
                    raised this question and he indicated that he felt there was no urgency about
                    the matter. He did, however, ask for a memorandum which he could study. I think
                    this must be most carefully drawn up and if George Allen,<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d510-f2"/> whom I presume <pb facs="0536" n="524" xml:id="pg524"/>
                    will prepare this for you, will check with Hayden Raynor<anchor n="63"
                        xml:id="d510-f3"/> he will give him some ideas which I have on the manner in
                    which the problem should be presented.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
